## How to File Your Monterey Lemon Law Claim

To file a lemon law claim in Monterey, you’ll need to

- Take your lemon vehicle to a repair facility- as per the manufacturer’s instructions.

- Collect all repair reports, including:

- A detailed description of the problems.

- The dates of each repair appointment.

- The total time your vehicle was in the shop for repairs.

- Copies of all invoices and receipts.

- Any correspondence with the manufacturer or dealer

- Talk to a competent Monterey lemon law attorney.

## California Lemon Law for Used Vehicles

California lemon laws also apply to defective pre-owned vehicles under certain conditions.

## Warranties on Pre-Owned Cars

Many used vehicles are sold with warranties lasting up to 30 days or 1,000 miles, whichever comes first. If your car develops a defect within this time frame, and the issue is covered under warranty, you may have a legitimate lemon law case.

Your Rights as a Consumer

Dealerships are legally required to either cover the cost of repairs or offer a buyback if your vehicle turns out to be a lemon. In most situations, you can recover the full purchase price, reimbursement for additional expenses, and attorney fees.

Buying a Vehicle ‘As-Is’

When you purchase a car “as-is,” you agree to take responsibility for its existing issues. Generally, as-is sales are not covered under California lemon law. However, this exemption only applies if the dealership clearly informs you that the vehicle is being sold “as-is” at the time of purchase.

